x86_64-linux  Ten names cxx1 emits and clang does not, every one a form nothing here calls: the complete-object constructors and destructor of A and V, which are only ever bases; the complete-object copy constructors of A, B, C, V and W, whose C2 forms the copy of D calls; and `_ZN1DC2ERKS_`, D's base-subobject copy where nothing derives from D. cxx1 emits C1 beside every C2 and C2 beside every C1; clang emits the form it uses. Every name this case is about agrees - `_ZTT1D`, `_ZTC1D0_1C`, `_ZTC1D16_1B`, `_ZTC1D64_1W`, the virtual thunks - and the tables' words are compared in the header of the .cpp.
arm64-darwin  The same less `__ZN1AD1Ev` and `__ZN1VD1Ev`, which this target's clang emits too; Mach-O's leading underscore on the rest.
